{"html":"<p>You write a counter with a normal variable, click the button, and nothing changes on screen. React doesn&#39;t watch your variables. To update the page, data has to live in <strong>state</strong>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"why-a-variable-isn-t-enough\">Why a Variable Isn&#39;t Enough</h2>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">function</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> Counter</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  let</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> count </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 0</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">button</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> onClick</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">={</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> count</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">++}</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">>Clicked </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">{</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">count</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">}</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> times&#x3C;/</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">button</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">>;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Two problems: changing <code>count</code> doesn&#39;t tell React to draw again, and even if it did, the function runs from the top and sets <code>count</code> back to 0.</p>\n<h2 id=\"usestate\">useState</h2>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">import</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> { useState } </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">from</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"react\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">function</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> Counter</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  const</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> [</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">count</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">setCount</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">] </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> useState</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">0</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">button</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> onClick</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">={</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> setCount</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(count </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">)</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">}</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">>Clicked </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">{</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">count</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">}</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> times&#x3C;/</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">button</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  );</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p><code>useState(0)</code> returns two things: the current value, and a function to change it. Calling <code>setCount</code>:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>stores the new value, and</li>\n<li>asks React to <strong>re-render</strong> the component: call the function again, now with the new value, and update the page.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Each component instance has its own state: two <code>&lt;Counter /&gt;</code>s count separately.</p>\n<h3 id=\"rules-of-hooks\">Rules of Hooks</h3>\n<p><code>useState</code> is a <strong>hook</strong>. Hooks must be called at the top level of a component, never inside <code>if</code>, loops or nested functions, because React tracks them by the order they&#39;re called.</p>\n<h2 id=\"state-is-a-snapshot\">State Is a Snapshot</h2>\n<p>During one render, <code>count</code> is a fixed value. Setting state doesn&#39;t change it right away:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">button</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> onClick</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">={</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">  setCount</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(count </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">  setCount</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(count </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">  setCount</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(count </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">}</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>One click adds <strong>1</strong>, not 3: all three calls read the same <code>count</code>, say 0, and set it to 1. When the next value depends on the previous one, pass a <strong>function</strong>:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">setCount</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">((</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">c</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> c </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">setCount</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">((</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">c</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> c </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">setCount</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">((</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">c</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> c </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">); </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// now one click adds 3</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>React runs these one after another, each with the latest value.</p>\n<h2 id=\"objects-and-arrays-replace-don-t-mutate\">Objects and Arrays: Replace, Don&#39;t Mutate</h2>\n<p>React compares the old and new state <strong>by reference</strong>. Changing an object in place keeps the same reference, so React may skip the update:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">const</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> [</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">user</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">setUser</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">] </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> useState</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">({ name: </span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"Ana\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, city: </span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"Lyon\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> });</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// Broken: same object, the screen doesn't change</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">user.city </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"Nice\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">setUser</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(user);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// Right: a new object with the change</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">setUser</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">({ </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">...</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">user, city: </span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"Paris\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> });</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>The same goes for arrays:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">setTodos</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">([</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">...</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">todos, newTodo]); </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// add</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">setTodos</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(todos.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">filter</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">((</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">t</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> t.id </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">!==</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> id)); </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// remove</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">setTodos</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(todos.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">map</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">((</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">t</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (t.id </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">===</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> id </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">?</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> { </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">...</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">t, done: </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">true</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> } </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">:</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> t))); </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// update</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><h2 id=\"don-t-store-what-you-can-compute\">Don&#39;t Store What You Can Compute</h2>\n<p>If a value can be computed from props or other state, compute it during render instead of storing it:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">const</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> [</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">first</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">setFirst</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">] </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> useState</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"Ana\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">const</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> [</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">last</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">setLast</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">] </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> useState</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"Martin\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">const</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> fullName</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> `${</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">first</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">} ${</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">last</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">}`</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">; </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// no state needed</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Duplicated state gets out of sync: one day <code>first</code> changes and <code>fullName</code> doesn&#39;t. The same applies to filtered lists, totals and counts.</p>\n<h2 id=\"lifting-state-up\">Lifting State Up</h2>\n<p>When two components need the same data, move the state to their closest common parent, and pass it down as props:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">function</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> ShoppingPage</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  const</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> [</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">cart</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">setCart</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">] </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> useState</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">([]);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    &#x3C;></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">      &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">ProductList</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> onAdd</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">={</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">product</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> setCart</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">([</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">...</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">cart, product])</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">}</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> /></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">      &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">CartSummary</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> items</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">={</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">cart</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">}</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> /></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    &#x3C;/></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  );</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p><code>ProductList</code> reports additions through <code>onAdd</code>; <code>CartSummary</code> shows the result. One source of truth, and both stay in sync.</p>\n<h2 id=\"where-state-should-live\">Where State Should Live</h2>\n<div data-table-scroll><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Data</th>\n<th>Put it in</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Used by one component</td>\n<td>That component&#39;s <code>useState</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Shared by siblings</td>\n<td>Their common parent, passed as props</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Needed by many components far apart</td>\n<td>Context, or a state library</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Computable from other data</td>\n<td>Nowhere: compute it during render</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Should survive a reload or be shareable</td>\n<td>The URL or storage</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"the-answer-in-short\">The Answer in Short</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Normal variables don&#39;t update the screen; <code>useState</code> stores data and re-renders on change.</li>\n<li>Call hooks at the top level of components, never in conditions or loops.</li>\n<li>State is a snapshot per render: use <code>setX((x) =&gt; …)</code> when the new value depends on the old one.</li>\n<li>Never mutate state: create new objects and arrays with spread, <code>map</code> and <code>filter</code>.</li>\n<li>Compute derived values instead of storing them, and lift shared state to the closest common parent.</li>\n</ol>\n"}